DESCRIPTION=AI tooling: reuse before you implement, plus the DevOps team skill. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md gain a Reuse before you implement section (research existing drivers, helpers and contracts in depth before writing new code, never two functions that do the same thing, extend instead of copying, add one shared helper and point every caller at it), mirrored for Cursor in .cursor/rules/reuse_before_implement.mdc. The devops-multi-agent-team skill from Homework Central is imported under .cursor/skills, .cursor/agents and .cursor/commands (goal, code-review, repro, triage, create-subagent), adapted to this repo: its Researcher writes a reuse map before a Coder starts, its Reviewers block duplicated new code, its CodeQL policy covers C and C++, and this repo's versioning and driver-boundary rules take precedence. .cursor/thoughts is git-ignored except its keepfile. First use (issue 384, D1): one shared hex codec, kernel/include/fl/hex.h (fl_hex_nibble, fl_hex_encode, fl_hex_decode, header-only), replaces the copies in user_db.c, bridge.c, kq_delivery.c and password_hash.cpp with identical output (checked against the old build with a fixed-salt password hash); new make test_hex. Rules: one .ver per PR, added with the first real push after QA and Security approval and only edited afterwards; the DevOps skill staffs 2 to 3 subagents per function and moves idle seats to busy ones. Not covered: Buildkite, Linear, Sonar, Snyk, Composio and Mainframe are named by the skill but optional here, and no CodeQL workflow exists in this repo yet. Other hex copies remain in server_shared_digest.c, net_wifi_db.c, disk.c, cluster.c, commands.c and lab_kq.c.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-10-28
